# Our workflow, not the product
#
# This repository is the product and the evidence it works — see
# DEVELOPMENT.md, "Repository artifacts". Instructions written to the agents
# that build it have an audience of us, not of a reader arriving at the
# project, so the tree refuses them rather than relying on anyone remembering.
#
# Not ignored, deliberately: scripts/ and .opencode/ are retained tooling —
# they implement the sandbox but are not themselves the security boundary;
# SECURITY.md ("External content and effects") owns what actually enforces
# isolation and requires a refused-crossing test to prove it, not a path or a
# test count. Findings under docs/ are evidence a reader can re-run. Both are
# product.
docs/tasks/
.impeccable/

# Skill tooling, not product
.agents/
.claude/
skills-lock.json
